WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Fixed and variable cost. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Separate cost behavior by activity

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Fixed cost stays roughly constant over a stated range; variable cost changes with the chosen activity driver.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: If setup is $80 and each unit adds $12 material, total cost for n units is 80+12n in this simple model.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Classification drill

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Teaching relationships only—not live quotes, prices, tax advice or forecasts.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Separate cost behavior by activity
